=============================
📌 EP04 – FOREACH LOOP IN DART
=============================

🔷 1️⃣ What is a forEach Loop?

A forEach loop is a function-based loop used to run code for every item in a list, set, or map.

✔ Shorter than normal for-loops
✔ Uses a callback function
✔ Very clean and readable

🔷 2️⃣ Basic Syntax

list.forEach((item) {
  // use item
});

item → each value

Code inside { } runs for every element

🔷 3️⃣ Example 1 – Simple List

List<String> names = ["Ram", "Shyam", "Mohan"];

// forEach loop
names.forEach((name) {
  print(name);  // Print each item
});

📌 Output:
Ram  
Shyam  
Mohan

🔷 4️⃣ Example 2 – Numbers

List<int> nums = [10, 20, 30];

nums.forEach((n) {
  print("Number: $n");   // Reading each value
});

🔷 6️⃣ Real-Life Example 2: Display Product Names

List<String> products = ["Mobile", "Laptop", "Watch"];

products.forEach((item) {
  print("Product: $item");
});


🔷 7️⃣ forEach with Set

Set<String> fruits = {"Apple", "Mango", "Banana"};

fruits.forEach((fruit) {
  print(fruit);
});


🔷 8️⃣ forEach with Map (Keys + Values)

✔ Loop only keys

Map<String, int> scores = {"Math": 95, "Science": 85};

scores.keys.forEach((key) {
  print("Subject: $key");
});

✔ Loop only values

scores.values.forEach((value) {
  print("Marks: $value");
});

✔ Loop entries (key + value)

scores.forEach((key, value) {
  print("$key = $value");
});


🔷 9️⃣ Important Notes
✔ forEach Cannot Be Stopped

You cannot use break or continue inside forEach.
Use normal for loop if you want to stop loop.

✔ Best for reading values

Not ideal when you need index number.

🟩 🔟 When should you use forEach?

✔ When you want clean readable code
✔ When you don't need index
✔ When you want functional programming style
✔ Best for lists, sets, maps
